        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01KqRLeDzD8d2qxu1VftoaXn",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022pages/tech/git-reflog.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Technology\\ntitle: Git Reflog\\ndescription: A local history of HEAD and branch ref positions that enables recovery after destructive operations like reset or rebase.\\ntimestamp: 2026-01-16T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - tech/Git\\n  - concept/Recovery\\n  - concept/Safety-Net\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single authoritative source describing reflog\\u0027s mechanism and scope; claims align with documented Git behavior.\\u0022\\nresource: https://git-scm.com/docs/git-reflog\\n---\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nGit\\u0027s **reflog** (reference log) records every position that HEAD and branch references\\nhave pointed to over time. This creates a local-only safety net that allows you to recover\\ncommits after destructive operations like reset or rebase would otherwise leave them\\nunreachable.\\n\\n## Recovery Use Case\\n\\nWhen you perform operations that rewrite history \\u2014 such as \\u0060git reset --hard\\u0060 or an\\ninteractive rebase \\u2014 commits that are no longer reachable from any branch tip appear\\nlost. Reflog preserves these dangling commits locally, making recovery possible.\\n\\n### Example: Recovering from a Bad Reset\\n\\nAfter an accidental \\u0060git reset --hard HEAD~5\\u0060, the last five commits vanish from your\\nbranch\\u0027s view:\\n\\n\\u0060\\u0060\\u0060bash\\n# Before: HEAD points to commit ABC123\\ngit reset --hard HEAD~5\\n# After: HEAD points to an ancestor; ABC123 is unreachable\\n\\n# Reflog shows where HEAD was:\\ngit reflog\\n# Output includes: abc123 HEAD@{0}: reset --hard HEAD~5\\n\\n# Recover by checking out the old HEAD or resetting to it:\\ngit reset --hard abc123\\n\\u0060\\u0060\\u0060\\n\\n### Example: Recovering from a Botched Rebase\\n\\nAn interactive rebase that drops the wrong commits or exits with an error can leave you\\nin an undesirable state. Reflog records the state before the rebase attempt:\\n\\n\\u0060\\u0060\\u0060bash\\ngit reflog\\n# Shows: commit-before-rebase HEAD@{1}: rebase: pick ...\\n# Shows: commit-at-rebase-start HEAD@{0}: rebase: \\u003Cdetached HEAD\\u003E\\n\\n# Reset to the state before the rebase started:\\ngit reset --hard commit-before-rebase\\n\\u0060\\u0060\\u0060\\n\\n## Scope and Limitations\\n\\nReflog is **local-only**: entries are stored on your machine and never pushed to a remote\\nrepository. On a fresh clone, reflog is empty \\u2014 you can only recover commits that you\\ncreated or fetched locally.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Git documentation on reflog and recovery.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
